#: apps/ops/tasks.py:162
msgid "Clean up unexpected jobs"
msgstr "Clean Up Anomalous Jobs"

#: apps/ops/tasks.py:164
msgid ""
"Due to exceptions caused by executing adhoc and playbooks in the Job Center, \n"
"        which result in the task status not being updated, the system will clean up abnormal jobs \n"
"        that have not been completed for more than 3 hours every hour and mark these tasks as \n"
"        failed"
msgstr ""
"Since executing quick commands or playbooks in the job center may produce "
"anomalies where task status is not updated to complete, the system will run "
"hourly to clean up anomalous jobs that have not completed for over 3 hours "
"and mark those tasks as failed."

#: apps/ops/tasks.py:177
msgid "Clean job_execution db record"
msgstr "Clear Job Center Execution History"

#: apps/ops/tasks.py:179
msgid ""
"Due to the execution of adhoc and playbooks in the Job Center, execution records will \n"
"        be generated. The system will clean up records that exceed the retention period every day \n"
"        at 2 a.m., based on the configuration of 'System Settings - Tasks - Regular clean-up - \n"
"        Job execution retention days'"
msgstr ""
"When the Job Center executes quick commands or playbooks, execution records "
"are generated. Based on the System Settings > Task List > Periodic Cleanup >"
" Job Center Execution History configuration, the system cleans up records "
"that have exceeded the retention time every day at 2:00 AM."

